          name: "Best Marble Sealer",
          item: "https://www.allmetalbrake.com/best-marble-sealer/",
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can any product make marble etch-proof?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No sealer stops etching on marble, because etching is a chemical reaction between acid and the calcite in the stone. Impregnators sit inside the pores and do not form a barrier on the surface. Some topical coatings and films claim etch resistance, but they change the look and feel of the stone and require professional application. For most homes, habits and polishing compound are the answer."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How frequently does marble need a fresh coat?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Test with water every six to twelve months. When water darkens the stone within about five minutes, reseal. Heavily used kitchen counters typically need it every one to two years, while bathroom vanities and floors often go two to three years. Premium fluoropolymer sealers can last longer than budget products on the same stone, which offsets part of their higher price."
          }
