          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is cultured marble the same as natural marble?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No. Cultured marble is a cast product made from crushed stone and resin with a gel coat on top, often used for one-piece vanity tops. It is not porous like natural stone and does not need or accept stone sealer. Clean it with non-abrasive cleaners and treat chips or dull spots as a gel-coat repair, not a sealing issue."
