          Marble owners usually buy sealer to fix the wrong problem. The dull, rough spots that appear where a glass of juice or a splash of vinegar sat are etches, a chemical reaction with the calcite in the stone, and sealer does almost nothing to stop them. What sealer does do, and does well, is keep coffee, wine and cooking oil from soaking in and leaving dark stains. Pick a product for that job, apply it correctly, and handle etching with habits and a polishing compound.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />


